maths/hexes/sphere.go Nearest: fi-float64(i0)+fj-float64(j0) > 1 => fi-float64(i0)+fj+float64(j0) > 1 :: the candidates choose where walk starts, and walk goes on to the nearest corner of the face from any start within three steps, which the walk test holds against every corner of the face; a changed candidate is at most two steps from the nearest, so the tile is the same and only the work differs. this rests on that test and the brute-force tests, not on a proof
