scene/medium/grove.go NewGrove: lo := tree.At.Sub(maths.V(tree.Radius, 0, tree.Radius)) => lo := tree.At.Sub(maths.V(tree.Radius, 1, tree.Radius)) :: lo.Y is never consumed: vertical bounds use GroundFloor, and the canopy index uses only lo.X and lo.Z
scene/medium/medium.go sphere: disc < 0 => disc <= 0 :: a zero discriminant is tangency with enter==leave; the mandatory leave>enter already returns false, whose endpoints callers ignore
scene/shape/group.go ValidPlacement: return !math.IsNaN(v) && !math.IsInf(v, 0) => return !math.IsNaN(v) && !math.IsInf(v, 1) :: the finite helper receives only Origin.Len() (nonnegative or NaN) and Scale (also checked for negativity); negative infinity remains refused in either case
scene/shape/group.go ValidPlacement: return math.Abs(x.Len()-1) < 1e-9 && math.Abs(y.Len()-1) < 1e-9 && math.Abs(z.Len()-1) < 1e-9 && math.Abs(x.Dot(y)) < 1e-9 && math.Abs(x.Dot(z)) < 1e-9 && math.Abs(y.Dot(z)) < 1e-9 && x.Cross(y).Dot(z) > 0 => return math.Abs(x.Len()-1) <= 1e-9 && math.Abs(y.Len()-1) < 1e-9 && math.Abs(z.Len()-1) < 1e-9 && math.Abs(x.Dot(y)) < 1e-9 && math.Abs(x.Dot(z)) < 1e-9 && math.Abs(y.Dot(z)) < 1e-9 && x.Cross(y).Dot(z) > 0 :: binary64 Len minus one cannot equal binary64(1e-9); see the exact lattice argument in doc/mutation-equivalence.md
