scene/shape/group.go ValidPlacement: return math.Abs(x.Len()-1) < 1e-9 && math.Abs(y.Len()-1) < 1e-9 && math.Abs(z.Len()-1) < 1e-9 && math.Abs(x.Dot(y)) < 1e-9 && math.Abs(x.Dot(z)) < 1e-9 && math.Abs(y.Dot(z)) < 1e-9 && x.Cross(y).Dot(z) > 0 => return math.Abs(x.Len()-1) < 1e-9 && math.Abs(y.Len()-1) < 1e-9 && math.Abs(z.Len()-1) < 1e-9 && math.Abs(x.Dot(y)) < 1e-9 && math.Abs(x.Dot(z)) < 1e-9 && math.Abs(y.Dot(z)) < 1e-9 && x.Cross(y).Dot(z) >= 0 :: the preceding unit and orthogonality guards exclude a singular basis; see the Gram-matrix bound in doc/mutation-equivalence.md
scene/shape/group.go memberBox: 8 => 9 :: i=8 has all three tested low bits clear and adds the already included local.Min corner
scene/shape/group.go memberBox: (i&1 != 0) => (!(i&1 != 0)) :: complementing one corner bit permutes the same eight transformed box corners; min/max enclosure is unchanged
scene/shape/group.go memberBox: i&1 != 0 => i&1 == 0 :: complementing one corner bit permutes the same eight transformed box corners; min/max enclosure is unchanged
scene/shape/group.go memberBox: i&1 != 0 => i&1 != 1 :: the low bit is either zero or one; complementing it visits the same eight corners in a different order
scene/shape/group.go memberBox: (i&2 != 0) => (!(i&2 != 0)) :: complementing one corner bit permutes the same eight transformed box corners; min/max enclosure is unchanged
