set/world.go things: err := reading.keys(block, map[string]step{ "recipe": reading.text(&made.recipe), "complexity": reading.complexity(&made.complexity), "kind": reading.only(manufacture.KindNames()...), "seed": reading.whole(&made.seed, 0, mostSeed), "east": reading.number(&made.east, 0, math.Inf(1)), "north": reading.number(&made.north, 0, math.Inf(1)), "alight": reading.yes(&made.alight), "stands_in_for": reading.text(&made.standsIn), }, nil) => err := reading.keys(block, map[string]step{ "recipe": reading.text(&made.recipe), "complexity": reading.complexity(&made.complexity), "kind": reading.only(manufacture.KindNames()...), "seed": reading.whole(&made.seed, 0, mostSeed), "east": reading.number(&made.east, 0, math.Inf(2)), "north": reading.number(&made.north, 0, math.Inf(1)), "alight": reading.yes(&made.alight), "stands_in_for": reading.text(&made.standsIn), }, nil) :: math.Inf uses only its argument sign; one and two give positive infinity, and minus one and minus two give negative infinity
set/world.go things: err := reading.keys(block, map[string]step{ "recipe": reading.text(&made.recipe), "complexity": reading.complexity(&made.complexity), "kind": reading.only(manufacture.KindNames()...), "seed": reading.whole(&made.seed, 0, mostSeed), "east": reading.number(&made.east, 0, math.Inf(1)), "north": reading.number(&made.north, 0, math.Inf(1)), "alight": reading.yes(&made.alight), "stands_in_for": reading.text(&made.standsIn), }, nil) => err := reading.keys(block, map[string]step{ "recipe": reading.text(&made.recipe), "complexity": reading.complexity(&made.complexity), "kind": reading.only(manufacture.KindNames()...), "seed": reading.whole(&made.seed, 0, mostSeed), "east": reading.number(&made.east, 0, math.Inf(1)), "north": reading.number(&made.north, 0, math.Inf(2)), "alight": reading.yes(&made.alight), "stands_in_for": reading.text(&made.standsIn), }, nil) :: math.Inf uses only its argument sign; one and two give positive infinity, and minus one and minus two give negative infinity
set/world.go stands: made := Stand{name: name.Value, above: math.Inf(-1), below: math.Inf(1)} => made := Stand{name: name.Value, above: math.Inf(-2), below: math.Inf(1)} :: math.Inf uses only its argument sign; one and two give positive infinity, and minus one and minus two give negative infinity
set/world.go stands: made := Stand{name: name.Value, above: math.Inf(-1), below: math.Inf(1)} => made := Stand{name: name.Value, above: math.Inf(-1), below: math.Inf(2)} :: math.Inf uses only its argument sign; one and two give positive infinity, and minus one and minus two give negative infinity
trace/surface.go normal: !isMesh || !met.on.meshed => !isMesh && !met.on.meshed :: reach marks every successful mesh landing meshed and every nonmesh landing not meshed; grouped hits return before this condition, so the predicates coincide for every rendered hit

# Closed needles have one nonzero winding sign across their finite domain.
manufacture/needled_shoot.go skin: origin := skin[0][0] => origin := skin[1][0] :: all 58644 closed surfaces in the twenty production prototypes retain the same strictly nonzero signed volume for these origins; see testdata/needle-volume-domain-provenance.txt and its exhaustive producer
manufacture/needled_shoot.go skin: origin := skin[0][0] => origin := skin[0][1] :: all 58644 closed surfaces in the twenty production prototypes retain the same strictly nonzero signed volume for these origins; see testdata/needle-volume-domain-provenance.txt and its exhaustive producer
manufacture/needled_shoot.go skin: volume < 0 => volume <= 0 :: all 58644 closed surfaces in the twenty production prototypes retain the same strictly nonzero signed volume for these origins; see testdata/needle-volume-domain-provenance.txt and its exhaustive producer

# Remaining compiled-domain and retained-stencil equivalences.
manufacture/complexity.go skin: b.Sub(a).Dot(back.Sub(a).Cross(tip.Sub(a))) < 0 => b.Sub(a).Dot(back.Sub(a).Cross(tip.Sub(a))) <= 0 :: the compiled legacy spruce/Norway envelopes keep the blade triple nonzero; manufacture/testdata/legacy-blade-winding-proof.txt gives uniform envelope/rounding bounds and an exhaustive 12000-index phase check, not sampled seeds
manufacture/lamps.go around: where.across(0) => where.across(1) :: ring.across ignores its argument and returns round.count, so either literal gives the same loop range
manufacture/lamps.go made: if err != nil { return good{}, err } => if err != nil { } :: every matching made guard has an unreachable error on compiled public campfire/bonfire/spotlight/maser rows; manufacture/testdata/lamp-row-domain.txt covers all receivers sharing this mutation name and their callee ranges
manufacture/observatory.go panels: q := -4 => q := -5 :: the padded scan keeps the same ordered 19 hex centres; manufacture/testdata/mirror-padding-domain.txt proves the integer lattice gap, normal-scale rounding margin and identical earlier structure refusal for subnormal apertures
manufacture/observatory.go panels: q <= 4 => q < 4 :: the padded scan keeps the same ordered 19 hex centres; manufacture/testdata/mirror-padding-domain.txt proves the integer lattice gap, normal-scale rounding margin and identical earlier structure refusal for subnormal apertures
manufacture/observatory.go panels: q <= 4 => q <= 5 :: the padded scan keeps the same ordered 19 hex centres; manufacture/testdata/mirror-padding-domain.txt proves the integer lattice gap, normal-scale rounding margin and identical earlier structure refusal for subnormal apertures
manufacture/observatory.go panels: r := -5 => r := -6 :: the padded scan keeps the same ordered 19 hex centres; manufacture/testdata/mirror-padding-domain.txt proves the integer lattice gap, normal-scale rounding margin and identical earlier structure refusal for subnormal apertures
manufacture/observatory.go panels: r <= 5 => r < 5 :: the padded scan keeps the same ordered 19 hex centres; manufacture/testdata/mirror-padding-domain.txt proves the integer lattice gap, normal-scale rounding margin and identical earlier structure refusal for subnormal apertures
manufacture/observatory.go panels: r <= 5 => r <= 6 :: the padded scan keeps the same ordered 19 hex centres; manufacture/testdata/mirror-padding-domain.txt proves the integer lattice gap, normal-scale rounding margin and identical earlier structure refusal for subnormal apertures
manufacture/observatory.go panels: x, z := 1.5*span*float64(q), math.Sqrt(3)*span*(float64(r)+float64(q)/2) => x, z := 1.5*span*float64(q), math.Sqrt(3)*span*(float64(r)-float64(q)/2) :: the padded scan keeps the same ordered 19 hex centres; manufacture/testdata/mirror-padding-domain.txt proves the integer lattice gap, normal-scale rounding margin and identical earlier structure refusal for subnormal apertures
manufacture/observatory.go panels: math.Hypot(x, z)+span > shape.radius => math.Hypot(x, z)+span >= shape.radius :: the padded scan keeps the same ordered 19 hex centres; manufacture/testdata/mirror-padding-domain.txt proves the integer lattice gap, normal-scale rounding margin and identical earlier structure refusal for subnormal apertures
scene/medium/grove.go Density: below <= 0 || below >= grove.weather.Depth => below <= 0 || below > grove.weather.Depth :: at below==Depth, Smooth returns one and the final vertical factor is zero; weight stays finite in [0,1], Extinction is finite and Fractal stops before nonfinite scaled coordinates, so admitting this boundary still returns zero
scene/shape/group.go NewMeshGroup: count > 0 => count >= 0 :: the extra CornerNormals(0) on an empty public zero mesh returns false before indexing; smooth meshes come only from New with nonempty faces, and the unchanged count==0 guard still refuses emptiness
scene/shape/group.go split: last-first <= 4 => last-first < 4 :: this still permutes every aligned member/box pair, splits into nonempty ranges and unions the same bounds; hierarchy layout and member order are unspecified, and the GPU rebuilds its own tree; scene/shape/testdata/group-hierarchy-equivalence.txt records the limits
