scene/shape/group.go split: (size.Y > size.X) => (!(size.Y > size.X)) :: this still permutes every aligned member/box pair, splits into nonempty ranges and unions the same bounds; hierarchy layout and member order are unspecified, and the GPU rebuilds its own tree; scene/shape/testdata/group-hierarchy-equivalence.txt records the limits
scene/shape/group.go split: if size.Y > size.X { axis = 1 } => if size.Y > size.X { } :: this still permutes every aligned member/box pair, splits into nonempty ranges and unions the same bounds; hierarchy layout and member order are unspecified, and the GPU rebuilds its own tree; scene/shape/testdata/group-hierarchy-equivalence.txt records the limits
scene/shape/group.go split: size.Y > size.X => size.Y >= size.X :: this still permutes every aligned member/box pair, splits into nonempty ranges and unions the same bounds; hierarchy layout and member order are unspecified, and the GPU rebuilds its own tree; scene/shape/testdata/group-hierarchy-equivalence.txt records the limits
