scene/shape/group.go split: size.Z > math.Max(size.X, size.Y) => size.Z >= math.Max(size.X, size.Y) :: this still permutes every aligned member/box pair, splits into nonempty ranges and unions the same bounds; hierarchy layout and member order are unspecified, and the GPU rebuilds its own tree; scene/shape/testdata/group-hierarchy-equivalence.txt records the limits
scene/shape/group.go split: size.Z > math.Max(size.X, size.Y) => size.Z <= math.Max(size.X, size.Y) :: this still permutes every aligned member/box pair, splits into nonempty ranges and unions the same bounds; hierarchy layout and member order are unspecified, and the GPU rebuilds its own tree; scene/shape/testdata/group-hierarchy-equivalence.txt records the limits
scene/shape/group.go split: size.Z > math.Max(size.X, size.Y) => size.Z > math.Min(size.X, size.Y) :: this still permutes every aligned member/box pair, splits into nonempty ranges and unions the same bounds; hierarchy layout and member order are unspecified, and the GPU rebuilds its own tree; scene/shape/testdata/group-hierarchy-equivalence.txt records the limits
